{"responseHeader":{"status":0,"QTime":10,"params":{"hl":"true","fl":"asset_id,subcollection,asset_type,asset_type_name,id,asset_language,url,updated_at,thumbnail,thumbnail_search,title_*,status,latest_activity,latest_activity_url,latest_activity_by,latest_activity_by_id,latest_activity_by_url,author_id,asked_by,asked_by_url,created_at,pinned,body_*","hl.requireFieldMatch":"false","hl.fragsize":"200","hl.usePhraseHighlighter":"true","q.op":"AND","fq":["subcollection:(discussions)","discussion-id:(cody)"],"hl.maxAlternateFieldLength":"300","group.ngroups":"true","defType":"lucene","hl.highlightAlternate":"false","hl.fl":"body_en,body_zh,body_ja,body_ko,body_fr,body_it,body_de,body_es,meta_description_en,meta_description_zh,meta_description_ja,meta_description_ko,meta_description_fr,meta_description_it,meta_description_de,meta_description_es","wt":"json","group.field":"container_uuid","group":"false","hl.alternateField":"body_en","group.limit":"50","start":"0","sort":"pinned desc,updated_at desc","rows":"4","hl.encoder":"html","facet.limit":"100","q":"*:*","group.format":"grouped","facet.mincount":"0","hl.method":"original","facet":"true","facet.sort":"count"}},"response":{"numFound":108,"start":0,"numFoundExact":true,"docs":[{"asset_id":"discussion:topic:864841","asset_type_name":["discussion"],"subcollection":["discussions"],"url":"/matlabcentral/discussions/cody/864841-welcome-to-the-cody-discussion-channel-please-read-before-posting","id":864841,"pinned":true,"thumbnail":"","author_id":6682740,"asked_by":"Chen Lin","asked_by_url":"/matlabcentral/profile/6682740","status":[""],"asset_language":"en","title_en":"Welcome to the Cody Discussion Channel! Please Read Before Posting","title_en_raw":"Welcome to the Cody Discussion Channel! Please Read Before Posting","body_en":"Hello and a warm welcome to everyone! We\u0026#39;re excited to have you in the Cody Discussion Channel. To ensure the best possible experience for everyone, it\u0026#39;s important to understand the types of content that are most suitable for this channel. Content that belongs in the Cody Discussion Channel: Tips \u0026amp; tricks: Discuss strategies for solving Cody problems that you\u0026#39;ve found effective. Ideas or suggestions for improvement: Have thoughts on how to make Cody better? We\u0026#39;d love to hear them. Issues: Encountering difficulties or bugs with Cody? Let us know so we can address them. Requests for guidance: Stuck on a Cody problem? Ask for advice or hints, but make sure to show your efforts in attempting to solve the problem first. General discussions: Anything else related to Cody that doesn\u0026#39;t fit into the above categories. Content that does not belong in the Cody Discussion Channel: Comments on specific Cody problems: Examples include unclear problem descriptions or incorrect testing suites. Comments on specific Cody solutions: For example, you find a solution creative or helpful. Please direct such comments to the Comments section on the problem or solution page itself. We hope the Cody discussion channel becomes a vibrant space for sharing expertise, learning new skills, and connecting with others. Welcome to the Cody Discussion Channel! Please Read Before Posting cody guidelines","body_en_raw":"Hello and a warm welcome to everyone! We\u0026#39;re excited to have you in the Cody Discussion Channel. To ensure the best possible experience for everyone, it\u0026#39;s important to understand the types of content that are most suitable for this channel. Content that belongs in the Cody Discussion Channel: Tips \u0026amp; tricks: Discuss strategies for solving Cody problems that you\u0026#39;ve found effective. Ideas or suggestions for improvement: Have thoughts on how to make Cody better? We\u0026#39;d love to hear them. Issues: Encountering difficulties or bugs with Cody? Let us know so we can address them. Requests for guidance: Stuck on a Cody problem? Ask for advice or hints, but make sure to show your efforts in attempting to solve the problem first. General discussions: Anything else related to Cody that doesn\u0026#39;t fit into the above categories. Content that does not belong in the Cody Discussion Channel: Comments on specific Cody problems: Examples include unclear problem descriptions or incorrect testing suites. Comments on specific Cody solutions: For example, you find a solution creative or helpful. Please direct such comments to the Comments section on the problem or solution page itself. We hope the Cody discussion channel becomes a vibrant space for sharing expertise, learning new skills, and connecting with others. Welcome to the Cody Discussion Channel! Please Read Before Posting cody guidelines","created_at":"2024-06-03T21:22:40Z","updated_at":"2026-06-05T02:54:00Z","asset_type":["1775"]},{"asset_id":"discussion:topic:889545","asset_type_name":["discussion"],"subcollection":["discussions"],"url":"/matlabcentral/discussions/cody/889545-check-out-cody-problems-created-by-minnolina","id":889545,"pinned":false,"thumbnail":"","author_id":5349647,"asked_by":"goc3","asked_by_url":"/matlabcentral/profile/5349647","status":[""],"asset_language":"en","title_en":"Check out Cody problems created by minnolina","title_en_raw":"Check out Cody problems created by minnolina","body_en":"As of August 2026, there are over 5,700 problems on Cody. Given that large quantity, and how long the site has been around, you might think that every good type of problem has been created. While there are far too many copies of simplistic problems, like adding two integers together, I recently stumbled across problems created by @minnolina. Today I finished all of the problems that this user has posted and I can recommend them as well done and worth your time. Whether or not you have solved any problems on Cody, right now is as good a time as any to sharpen your coding skills, and the problems created by minnolina provide a very good sampling of quality Cody problems. Check out Cody problems created by minnolina cody problem algorithm practice exercise kata unique well done minnolina quality","body_en_raw":"As of August 2026, there are over 5,700 problems on Cody. Given that large quantity, and how long the site has been around, you might think that every good type of problem has been created. While there are far too many copies of simplistic problems, like adding two integers together, I recently stumbled across problems created by @minnolina. Today I finished all of the problems that this user has posted and I can recommend them as well done and worth your time. Whether or not you have solved any problems on Cody, right now is as good a time as any to sharpen your coding skills, and the problems created by minnolina provide a very good sampling of quality Cody problems. Check out Cody problems created by minnolina cody problem algorithm practice exercise kata unique well done minnolina quality","created_at":"2026-08-17T19:00:59Z","updated_at":"2026-08-17T19:00:59Z","asset_type":["1775"]},{"asset_id":"discussion:topic:888464","asset_type_name":["discussion"],"subcollection":["discussions"],"url":"/matlabcentral/discussions/cody/888464-flagging-solutions","id":888464,"pinned":false,"thumbnail":"","author_id":15363629,"asked_by":"Christian Schröder","asked_by_url":"/matlabcentral/profile/15363629","status":[""],"asset_language":"en","title_en":"Flagging solutions","title_en_raw":"Flagging solutions","body_en":"It used to be possible to flag solutions, e.g. as \u0026quot;hack/cheat\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;needs rescoring\u0026quot;, and so on. Ever since the update to Cody\u0026#39;s design, this has been missing. Are there any plans to bring it back? Flagging solutions Hi Christian. I can see the Flag button is still there (see the screenshot below). Please let me know if you can see it on your end. ","body_en_raw":"It used to be possible to flag solutions, e.g. as \u0026quot;hack/cheat\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;needs rescoring\u0026quot;, and so on. Ever since the update to Cody\u0026#39;s design, this has been missing. Are there any plans to bring it back? Flagging solutions Hi Christian. I can see the Flag button is still there (see the screenshot below). Please let me know if you can see it on your end. ","latest_activity":"Replied","latest_activity_url":"http://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/discussions/cody/888464-flagging-solutions#reply_2624714","latest_activity_by":"Chen Lin","latest_activity_by_id":6682740,"latest_activity_by_url":"/matlabcentral/profile/6682740","created_at":"2026-06-02T06:40:09Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T14:21:47Z","asset_type":["1775"]},{"asset_id":"discussion:topic:888447","asset_type_name":["discussion"],"subcollection":["discussions"],"url":"/matlabcentral/discussions/cody/888447-solutions-for-cody-problems","id":888447,"pinned":false,"thumbnail":"","author_id":39800218,"asked_by":"Rachel","asked_by_url":"/matlabcentral/profile/39800218","status":[""],"asset_language":"en","title_en":"Solutions for Cody problems","title_en_raw":"Solutions for Cody problems","body_en":"","body_en_raw":"","latest_activity":"님이 답글을 추가함:","latest_activity_url":"http://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/discussions/cody/888447-solutions-for-cody-problems#reply_2624692","latest_activity_by":"Chen Lin","latest_activity_by_id":6682740,"latest_activity_by_url":"/matlabcentral/profile/6682740","created_at":"2026-05-31T20:44:56Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T13:46:40Z","asset_type":["1775"]}]},"facet_counts":{"facet_queries":{},"facet_fields":{},"facet_ranges":{},"facet_intervals":{},"facet_heatmaps":{}},"highlighting":{"discussion:topic:864841":{"body_en":["Hello and a warm welcome to everyone! We\u0026#x27;re excited to have you in the Cody Discussion Channel. To ensure the best possible experience for everyone, it\u0026#x27;s important to understand the types of content that are most suitable for this channel. Content that belongs in the Cody Discussion Channel: Tips \u0026amp; "],"body_zh":["Hello and a warm welcome to eve